The legal texts are official texts of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela, published in the Gaceta Oficial de la
República Bolivariana de Venezuela:

  Constitución de la República Bolivariana de Venezuela, Gaceta Oficial N° 5.908 Extraordinario, 19 February 2009,
  as hosted by the Instituto Nacional de Estadística (https://ine.gob.ve), and the text of 1999 as published by the
  Asamblea Nacional (https://www.asambleanacional.gob.ve), and the Constitución de 1961 with its two
  enmiendas as transcribed by the Tribunal Supremo de Justicia (https://www.tsj.gob.ve), retrieved 28 October 2026.

Venezuela's Ley sobre el Derecho de Autor (1993) is understood to exclude laws, regulations, judicial decisions and
other official acts from protection (art. 11); that reading has not been checked against the gazette text here. The
texts are reproduced as official acts, with the attribution above.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; lines missing from the INE copy of the gazette were restored from the
Asamblea Nacional text (listed in REPRODUCE.md); the "(Ver Enmienda N° 1 ...)" notes were removed from the text and the
amended articles given the wording of the Enmienda; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the
acts that made each change. The wording of the law was not otherwise changed. No Venezuelan authority endorses this
repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
